"""
ata - private remote access without root, VPN, or open ports.

Transport: zrok2 private share (OpenZiti), free plan.
Both the server and the client only make outbound connections. Neither
side opens a port to the internet. Shares are closed by default: only
environments in the same zrok account can access them.

Usage:
    ./ata init          # configure this machine (server or client)
    ./ata up            # start gateway + shares (server) or accesses (client)
    ./ata status
    ./ata down
    ./ata doctor
    ./ata export        # generate a client bundle (contains a secret)
    ./ata --help

Requirements: Python 3.8+, Linux x86_64/arm64/armv7, outbound HTTPS to
api-v2.zrok.io and the zrok routers. Root is not required.
"""

